# the argument of berkeley-heat-pain.md by rule (phil/skeleton): connectives from the parse, an atom to each clause
atom	vehement_intense_degree	but is the most vehement and intense degree of heat a very great pain ?
atom	hyl	HYL
atom	deny(x)	x: can deny it
atom	phil	PHIL
atom	unperceiv_thing_capable	and is any unperceiving thing capable of pain or pleasure ?
atom	certainly	no certainly
atom	material_substance_senseless	is your material substance a senseless being ?
atom	endow_sense_perception	a being endowed with sense and perception
atom	senseless_doubt	it is senseless without doubt
atom	subject_pain	it can therefore be the subject of pain ?
atom	mean	by no means
atom	acknowledge_small_pain	you acknowledge this to be small pain
atom	perceiv_sense	nor perceived by sense ?
atom	grant	I grant it
P1	S1	!vehement_intense_degree
P2	S2	hyl
P3	S3	(all x: !deny(x))
P4	S4	phil
P5	S5	unperceiv_thing_capable
P6	S6	hyl
P7	S7	certainly
P8	S8	phil
P9	S9	(material_substance_senseless | endow_sense_perception)
P10	S10	hyl
P11	S11	senseless_doubt
P12	S12	phil
P13	S13	!subject_pain
P14	S14	hyl
P15	S15	mean
P16	S16	phil
P17	S17	!acknowledge_small_pain
P18	S17	(!acknowledge_small_pain -> perceiv_sense)
C	S17	perceiv_sense
P19	S18	hyl
P20	S19	grant
# rules tool=phil/skeleton date=2026-10-20
